{"schema_version":"1.0.0","document_id":"87849141442eb95c9a8b4434336396b56dd022d90437cbc47f353ce2fbaf1acc","company_key":"advanced-energy-industries-inc-common-stock","company_name":"Advanced Energy Industries Inc.","source_id":"advanced-energy-industries-inc-common-stock-rss-7c5b1a0c72ca","source_kind":"rss","canonical_url":"https://www.advancedenergy.com/en-us/about/news/blog/tegam-voltmeter-case-sports-safety-features/","observed_url":"https://www.advancedenergy.com/en-us/about/news/blog/tegam-voltmeter-case-sports-safety-features/","title":"Voltmeter Case Sports Safety Features","summary":"Advanced Energy offers a new Cordura Nylon Carrying Case to improve worker safety.","body_text":"Home / About AE / News & Events / Blog / Voltmeter Case Sports Safety Features Voltmeter Case Sports Safety Features Posted November 06, 2012 by Advanced Energy Editor Contains no metal, making it safer around energized conductors Advanced Energy offers a new Cordura Nylon Carrying Case to improve worker safety. The model 1204A case will fit any of the three Safety Volt Meters, models 110A, 122, and 125 (note, all SVM models are now discontinued). The sturdy case, has several features that help users make safer measurements: No metal parts, making it safe for use around energized conductors. Buckled shoulder strap for carrying and clipping over a pipe or pole, allowing a user to use both hands for making a measurement. Magnet in the cover flap to allow a user to attach it to any steel surface. Share Advanced Energy Editor Advanced Energy More posts by Advanced Energy Editor Browse Categories A-Z Latest from AE News & Press Releases Videos Trade Shows & Conferences Webinars Join Our Mailing List Subscribe Recent Posts View on X","published_at":"2012-11-06T00:00:00+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-07-20T23:21:13.689408+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-07-28T22:27:50.599687+00:00","last_updated_at":"2026-08-20T03:25:12.389867+00:00","content_hash":"sha256:74b0e4abdb9accb879b146a4c21e46461814a88d